                        "review": "confusing, weird, unfun? there's a million options, and while the mechanics are straightforward, you just feel like you chain levels without purpose. scoring feels pointless, stage design is an afterthought, and bosses get exhausting real quick. on top of that, nothing is explained to you! you can just go in some weird chronicle mode and pick a route / area from some weird grid but none of it makes sense. there's some seemingly classic arcade mode but it also feels very dry. this is a bit more personal but not a fan of the type of bullets in this game (everything is pencil thin) and just adds to the lack of impact i can feel in the game.\n\nthe best part of the game is the DLC ships which unfortunately cost you extra money. they bring a little something that make it more fun to play compared to the rest of the game. i might as well just play their original game though!\n\nif you want a chill laid back time where you can just boot up whatever... it's there? but i just have no idea why i would ever want to go back to this personally, and don't really recommend it unless you get it on sale.\n\ncool soundtrack though!",
